-- examples/checks/ds-tree-demand-edge.rofl — the ds_tree_demand_edge world: the edge relation of a declared tree is answered on demand (a head variable its body does not bind), and the world keeps no witness. The closure is then rows, not the tree's answer: the engine reads which relations are answered on demand AFTER the program is prepared, and read before, it answered the closure from a forest of no stored edge.
sealed(provenance).
tree dtd_e(P, C) closure dtd_w.
dtd_q(a). dtd_q(b).
dtd_bs(a, b). dtd_bs(b, c).
dtd_e(X, Y) :- dtd_q(X).
dtd_r(D) :- dtd_w(a, D), dtd_bs(a, D).
alarm(dtd_lost).
dtd_lost(r) :- not dtd_r(b).
